From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:16:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] [Spec] copy_match and copy_select (TileLang), the copy
 drafter

copy_match: for each request of the batch, over its own history up to its
length, the latest window end per level (m, 2m, ..., 256) whose preceding tokens
equal the context's tail; (requests, 32) blocks, no atomics. copy_select: the
request's copy state updated from this step's verification (the cap doubles
from initial_drafts after a fully accepted copy, returns there after a
rejection or a step without a copy; decayed acceptance counts), then the
longest level's latest source: up to the cap of its continuation at the
acceptance estimate, or DSpark's drafts; the planned confidences and the
allocation the scheduler lays out two steps on. CopyDrafter owns the per-slot
state, reset with each request, and declares both kernels.

Tests: both kernels against numpy references (contexts to 20000 tokens,
vocabularies 3 to 129280, any slot order), a slot's stale tokens and other
requests' text never propose, CUDA-graph replay, the proposer against the
design's walk (experiments/2026-10-26-suffix-drafter variants.py, exact m16 k16
grow with the allocation lag), a slot's copy state reset, and temperature-0
text through the greedy verification kernels identical with and without copy
drafts.
